I Chisholm writes:
>Oh, an idea for a new monster, dev team. As a punishment for angering
>the gods, the harpies should be sent to haunt you. They would be
>extremely fast (winged) with claw and talon attacks and eat any edibles
>found. They would have a high chance (8/10?) of following you down
>levels and would be very difficult to kill except by using
>nets/paralysis/wands or some such 'projectile' attack. Personally, I
>think this would be more punishing then aggravate monster.

This is a great idea!  Make them use the same algorithm that unicorns do
to avoid getting in the character's line of fire.  Let them pick up darts
and knives and such to throw at the player to discourage attempts to nickle
and dime them to death.  Make the character use wand charges or spells!
Give harpies occasional teleportation to make sure they can get ahead of
the character on virgin levels.  Of course, they have hands so they will
open doors to get through them.  Make their corpses always rancid, even 
when fresh.  And most important, make sure they clean out *every bit* of 
edible substance (including corpses) that they can find!  This would be a 
great punishment, the more so because super-fighters who can laugh off most 
`punishment' still have to eat!

There might even subtypes of harpies -- maybe some would collect normal
stuff (potions, scrolls, etc.) in addition to weapons and food.  These would
be punishment indeed!

-Leonard

